# One line. Run from the repo root by `orgasmic verify TASK-2QK4P.1`.
#
# `env -u ...` because a dispatch leaks its run id and home into subprocesses,
# and these tests build their own Home under a temp root that must see neither.
#
# The WHOLE `recovery_claim::` filter rather than the failing tests alone,
# because the finding is about the WIDTH of a branch and the width is only
# legible from what stays green beside the red — above all
# `committed_claim_survives_a_catalog_that_invalidated_its_live_replacement`,
# the 409 the injected predicate genuinely fixes. `expect-red` names every test
# the injection moves and why.
#
# `--test-threads=1` because every one of these tests writes a claim directory
# and a session directory under its own tempdir and the panic text must be
# attributable to one test.
env -u ORGASMIC_RUN_ID -u ORGASMIC_HOME cargo test -p orgasmic-daemon --lib recovery_claim:: -- --test-threads=1
